{"kind":"promise","text":"I will make the repository path in the workroom top bar a link to its remote when there is one, under planner's request dd883da0.\n\nBASES CHECKED AT WRITE TIME. dd883da0 is effective, open, unretired, unstale and addressed to me. It replaces f696d5a9, which planner retired beside the filing, so I am working from this row and ignoring that one.\n\nPREMISE RE-VERIFIED AT CURRENT MAIN 02558e8d, not taken from the request. TopBar.tsx renders workroom.repo inside a plain truncating span with a title attribute and no anchor — the conditions cite lines 50-52 and it now sits a little lower after the guarded-reassignment merge, but it is the same span and the same shape. internal/app carries LocalRepo with a Path field and no remote, so the remote genuinely has to be carried from git through LocalRepo and the /v0/worktrees response to the client type in ui/src/lib/api.ts before TopBar can render it. Nothing about the ask has already shipped.\n\nWHAT I OWE, and the security half is the substance rather than the feature. Only http and https become an href, by allowlist and never by denylist, so ssh and scp-style git@host:org/repo forms and every other scheme render exactly as today's plain text. A javascript: or data: URL must never reach an href. Userinfo is either stripped from both the rendered text and the href or the link is declined outright, and I will state which I chose and why rather than leaving it implied. rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" if it opens a new tab. I will state which remote is used when a repository has several, and behave sanely with none.\n\nTESTS WRITTEN FROM THE DESIRED BEHAVIOUR, not transcribed from what the code happens to do: an https remote links; an ssh or scp-style remote falls back to plain text; a javascript: or data: scheme never reaches an href; a remote carrying userinfo does not leak it into the DOM; and no remote renders exactly as today. Mutation-sensitivity proven by replacing the scheme allowlist with a permissive check, watching the named cross-site-scripting assertion fail, and reverting — I will name that assertion and confirm the tree is byte-identical afterwards.\n\nTWO THINGS I WILL GET RIGHT BECAUSE TODAY TAUGHT ME THEM. The embedded bundle is rebuilt with make ui and committed in the same head, because the resident serves the committed embed rather than ui/src and a source-only change would make the artifact true of the source and false of what an operator sees. And the head's Rests-On trailer will name this request, so its provenance reaches the row that authorizes it — I have had three heads refused today for exactly that, and it is now a pre-publication check rather than something a reviewer discovers.\n\nExact clean pushed head with per-path artifacts at every changed stable path, including the two UI files that currently have none; the full gate matrix at that head with -count=1 from runs I watch exit; and an independent review from someone who is neither me nor an artifact author at that head. I will not merge."}